answer:
The Joint Consultative Committee for the Administration of the Collective Agreement is addressed in Article 2.60 of the Laurentian University Faculty Association Collective Agreement for both the years 2017-2020 and 2008-11. According to this article, the committee is composed of three representatives from each party:

* The President of the Union and the Vice-President, Academic or their respective designates;
* One officer of LUFA (Laurentian University Faculty Association);
* One Dean appointed by the Vice-President, Academic;
* One appointee from each Party.

The Committee aims to maintain and develop a spirit of cooperation and mutual respect between the Parties, facilitate better working relationships, discuss, review, and make recommendations on matters of concern to either Party. The Committee shall meet at least once in November and once in February, and at other times when deemed useful or necessary by mutual agreement of the Parties (Source: Collective Agreement 2017-2020, Article 2.60).

In addition, the Parties are authorized from time to time to enter into Memoranda of Agreement with regard to the Collective Agreement, and other representatives may be authorized to sign these Memoranda of Agreement (Source: Collective Agreement 2017-2020, Article 2.60). The Committee shall determine its own procedures subject to the provision that a quorum shall consist of at least two (2) representatives of each Party (Source: Collective Agreement 2017-2020, Article 2.60). The Committee shall not have the power to add to or modify the terms of this Collective Agreement (Source: Collective Agreement 2017-2020, Article 2.60).

